Task: Verificación en dispositivo (NFR6) (Fase 6, pattern-copy_20260910)

`device-verification.md` records the thirteen acceptance criteria against the
iPad with the BeatStep Pro, written from what was observed — which is why it
contains a failure.

Criterion 8 failed: the copy happened but the pasted material did not sound
until the Pattern was triggered by hand again. Investigating it turned up a
second, worse half — the live copy of the Pattern kept the previous material, so
the first knob turn wrote it back over the paste — and showed criterion 5 had
been passed on incomplete evidence: only the grid was checked, and the grid reads
the Bank, which was telling the truth. The `track` screen was not.

Fase 7 fixed both halves and the four re-checks are recorded too. The document
also states what was not measured (no jitter, NFR4) and the method lesson: no
test pass would have found this — the live copy lives in `App`, which is not
measured, and the missing rule did not exist in `Engine` yet to be tested. What
found it was one concrete case with the iPad in front; what closed it was moving
the rule down to `Engine` so it is tested from now on.

